<h1>TPageLoadTime</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="4.2.0" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.WebControls.TPageLoadTime" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TPageLoadTime</tt> displays the time the server spent on the current request. The
control measures from the moment the web server received the request to the moment the
control renders, and writes the result in seconds with five decimal places.
</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TPageLoadTime /&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<p class="block-content">
The control extends <tt>TLabel</tt> and renders a <tt>&lt;span&gt;</tt>, so
<tt>CssClass</tt>, <tt>Style</tt>, and the other label properties apply. The control
replaces the label's <tt>Text</tt> with the measured time, so setting <tt>Text</tt> has no
effect.
</p>

<h2>Placement</h2>

<p class="block-content">
The reported time covers the work done before the control renders. A control near the end
of the page template therefore reports a longer time than one near the top. Place the
control at the foot of a layout to measure as much of the page as possible.
</p>

<h2>Naming the unit</h2>

<p class="block-content">
The control appends the <tt>SecondSuffix</tt> property to the number. The property
defaults to <tt>s</tt>.
</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TPageLoadTime SecondSuffix=" seconds" /&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<p class="block-content">
The suffix passes through <tt>Prado::localize()</tt>, so a translated application takes
the suffix from its message catalogue.
</p>

